(6287747, 929477, 120798, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> some people hate the term "shoehorn" but some shots are just that. I think when you have to kind of bludgeon the viewer over the head with the title, thats the first indicator. its a nice shot that stands on its own, but does not evoke the feeling of work for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the feedback. I totally see what you are saying about the shoehorn thing, and that will help me with my next challenges. However, I feel it is better to have an image that is not so obvious, can be interpreted in different ways, and has a tittle which illustrates the photographer''s own point of view of the challenge. Rather than having a picture that itself bludgeons the viewer over the head with work symbols such as hammers, nails, and men doing construction. I guess that is why the winners did neither symbol nor tittle bludgeoning :-).</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: some people hate the term "shoehorn" but some shots are just that. I think when you have to kind of bludgeon the viewer over the head with the title, thats the first indicator. its a nice shot that stands on its own, but does not evoke the feeling of work for me.   Thanks for the feedback. I totally see what you are saying about the shoehorn thing, and that will help me with my next challenges. However, I feel it is better to have an image that is not so obvious, can be interpreted in different ways, and has a tittle which illustrates the photographer''s own point of view of the challenge. Rather than having a picture that itself bludgeons the viewer over the head with work symbols such as hammers, nails, and men doing construction. I guess that is why the winners did neither symbol nor tittle bludgeoning :-).', '2011-01-19 02:30:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6287760, 929693, 49109, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Enzo, on your HM (Mojo gone? Never!). Looks like the spider web helped a we bit :)</td>', 'Congrats, Enzo, on your HM (Mojo gone? Never!). Looks like the spider web helped a we bit :)', '2011-01-19 02:54:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6287761, 929620, 114285, '<td valign="top">Congrats i loved this, and well done for getting a a ribbon after being away for a while.</td>', 'Congrats i loved this, and well done for getting a a ribbon after being away for a while.', '2011-01-19 02:54:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6287771, 929478, 3585, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fantac:</b></div><hr/><i> I made an interesting observation...top 6 entries in this challenge are B&amp;W. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>But the "colorists" took a shameless revenge in the "work" challenge; all in sweet shades of pink. Diabetics beware!</td>', 'Originally posted by fantac: I made an interesting observation...top 6 entries in this challenge are B&W.   But the "colorists" took a shameless revenge in the "work" challenge; all in sweet shades of pink. Diabetics beware!', '2011-01-19 03:12:53.000000', NULL, 0),
