(6288274, 929449, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by njsabs:</b></div><hr/><i> I have been here before on JPL''s Open House event.  I used to go every year.  Congrats on top 10.  You are on a roll!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, they hold open houses every year usually sometime in May.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-01-19 13:52:21.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by njsabs: I have been here before on JPL''s Open House event.  I used to go every year.  Congrats on top 10.  You are on a roll!!   Yeah, they hold open houses every year usually sometime in May.', '2011-01-19 12:03:10.000000', '2011-01-19 13:52:21.000000', 0),
(6288282, 929449, 112972, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tome:</b></div><hr/><i> You work here?! Wow! So you already are at your dream job. I guessed this was from the viewing gallery (although the angle looks a bit lower than other photos I''ve seen, you might be somewhere else with your employee pass :). Anyway, not only a great location but a perfect shot too. I gave you a 10.<br/>My son just saw this photo and reminded me that he has his name on that chip going to Mars. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That is cool.  I will provide that link for whomever that is interested to have their name signed on a microchip on this rover going to Mars.  Here it is:<br/> <br/>//marsparticipate.jpl.nasa.gov/msl/participate/sendyourname/<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-01-19 12:28:12.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by tome: You work here?! Wow! So you already are at your dream job. I guessed this was from the viewing gallery (although the angle looks a bit lower than other photos I''ve seen, you might be somewhere else with your employee pass :). Anyway, not only a great location but a perfect shot too. I gave you a 10.My son just saw this photo and reminded me that he has his name on that chip going to Mars.   That is cool.  I will provide that link for whomever that is interested to have their name signed on a microchip on this rover going to Mars.  Here it is: //marsparticipate.jpl.nasa.gov/msl/participate/sendyourname/', '2011-01-19 12:09:27.000000', '2011-01-19 12:28:12.000000', 0),
(6288297, 929620, 68947, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  I love that this is a soft focus and so lightly contrasted!  It suits it perfectly.  Too often, we get marked down for pieces that are soft focused and aren''t overly contrasted.  It''s a shame because these types of photos are BEAUTIFUL!  Well done. :)</td>', 'Congrats!  I love that this is a soft focus and so lightly contrasted!  It suits it perfectly.  Too often, we get marked down for pieces that are soft focused and aren''t overly contrasted.  It''s a shame because these types of photos are BEAUTIFUL!  Well done. :)', '2011-01-19 12:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
